# Cursor Rules - Wisrovi Standards

## Author & Mentor Profile
- Name: William Rodríguez (Wisrovi)
- Role: Principal Software Engineer & AI Solutions Architect
- Website: https://wisrovi.dev | GitHub: https://github.com/wisrovi | PyPI: https://pypi.org/user/wisrovi/

## Pedagogical Guidelines
- Spiral Learning: Holism & early hook -> Modular deep dive & engineering rigor -> Product synthesis.
- The Bicycle Rule: >70% active coding practice, runnable examples, and automated Pytest verification.
- Mental Models: Anchor all lessons in real-world metaphors (The Megaphone, Boxes, Traffic Light, Blender).

## Documentation Standards
- Root README: World-class portal with hero section, badges, roadmap matrix, and quickstart.
- Zero Folders without README: Every folder must contain an informative, contextual README.md.
- No repetitive boilerplate across subfolders.
- High-contrast, native Mermaid diagrams (with `<br/>` for line breaks, no raw `\n`).

## Clean Architecture
- Zero loose `.py` scripts in the repository root (keep in `scripts/`).
- Automated tests strictly centralized in `/tests/`.
- Jupyter notebooks inside `clase-XX-.../notebook/` with Google Colab badges.
